From 4547c31fb3787c5ceb7cf15b7cfc427a9651975a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 16:29:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www/httpd: one Backup & Restore master panel owns every
 backup surface

The Reaper settings (JSON) export/import moves off Reaper_Storage.asp and
into the injected card on Administration > Restore/Save/Upload, which is
rebuilt as a master Backup & Restore panel: an intro line that says which
of the two files does which job, side-by-side sections for the full .rbk
backup (everything, model-locked, one reboot) and the portable settings
file (Reaper features only, no reboot), each with its scope badge,
description and guidance note, one shared pending-restore banner and one
message line, and a ? link to the owner's guide (2.5 Two backups, not one).

The settings wiring that lived duplicated on the Storage page (export,
import, pending check, complete-restore) now exists once, in the
reaper_inject.c mode-4 block - pure logic, every string still rides a
hidden span in the fragment, new XHRs on onloadend. The Storage page keeps
only the long-term store selection and data export, as its header comment
always claimed. Stock page stays byte-pristine.

Four new tokens (RBKP_15-18: panel title, chooser line, two scope badges)
appended to all 25 dicts in lockstep (6746 -> 6750). Everything else
reuses the existing RBKP_1-14 + RDST_68-77 strings.

Validated: extracted macro JS parses under node --check with every span
and element id resolving against the fragment; macro region compiles
standalone; reaper_langcheck 0 breakers / 22 pages; ASCII-clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
